{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>For they are a nation void of counsel</b>. The entire passage concerns the enemy mentioned above, according to the words of Rabbi Nechemiah (Sifrei 28). And the sense of <b>For their rock is not like our Rock</b> is likewise the words of the enemy. Scripture says that they should have thought about and understood this deed done to Israel, for it is the doing of HaShem on account of their iniquity, and they should discern from it the end of their own souls, for so will He do in the end to all the nations, since they rebel against HaShem more than Israel. They should have understood and said: How could one pursue a thousand of Israel, if not because their Rock has sold them? For their Rock is mighty and possesses the ability to help and deliver more than our rock. Our enemies were at first presumptuous against us, to do with us as they wished, and now why do a thousand flee from before us at the rebuke of one man? Were it not for their mighty Rock who sold them and brought faintness into their heart — and they fell, with no pursuer. פְּלִילִים (presumptuous): from the language of <b>אֲשֶׁר פִּלַּלְתְּ לַאֲחוֹתֵךְ</b> (Ezekiel 16:52, \"you judged your sister\"), <b>וַיַּעֲמֹד פִּנְחָס וַיְפַלֵּל</b> (Psalms 106:30, \"Pinchas stood and interceded\")."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The citation of Psalms 106:30 reads ויפלל ('and interceded') in the received text; Ramban cites it with the same root to illustrate the sense of פלילים."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:58:24.704955976Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}